# Docs and Devpost rules

- Plain, specific, honest. Say what works live and what is a stretch. Never inflate what the team built.
- No em dashes. Short sentences. Numbers with units (accuracy %, latency s, speed).
- Map the story to the judging criteria in the onsite packet: Creativity, Utility, Charity, Avidity.
- Devpost tracks: exactly one main track (Healthcare) plus special tracks we actually qualify for.
- The demo must fit in 2 minutes: problem in one sentence, who it is for, live demo, what we learned, what's next.
